The STAR Barrel Electromagnetic Calorimeter is also used to distinguish \(e^{\pm}\) from hadrons. The BEMC is approximately 20 radiation lengths deep, the depth required

Figure 3.14: The ratio \(p/E_{Tower}\) vs. \(p_{T}\) for tracks in MB triggered events that pass all other \(e^{\pm}\) identification cuts. Most \(e^{\pm}\) have \(p/E_{Tower}\approx 1/c\).

