The partial efficiencies have been calculated for each of the \(e^{\pm}\) identification cuts. Some of these calculations are presented in this section, while additional material is presented in Section C.1.2. Figures 4.11 through 4.20 show example distributions for each quantity (in one \(p_{T}\) bin) and the calculated partial efficiencies for each cut. Partial efficiencies for minimum-bias \(e^{\pm}\) are shown for \(p_{T}<4\,\mbox{GeV}\!/c\), while partial efficiencies for high-tower triggered \(e^{\pm}\) are shown for \(p_{T}>4\,\mbox{GeV}\!/c\).

