\[Y_{D,B}=Y_{HF}-B_{J/\psi}-B_{\Upsilon}=N_{EC}-B_{LFP}-B_{LFN}-B_{D-Y}-B_{J/\psi }-B_{\Upsilon}, \tag{9.6}\]

where \(B_{J/\psi}\) (\(B_{\Upsilon}\)) is the yield of photonic \(e^{\pm}\) from the decays of \(J/\psi\) (\(\Upsilon\)). Figure 9.2 shows the corrected \(e^{\pm}\) yields \(N_{EC}\), \(Y_{HF}\), and \(Y_{D,B}\) for the 0-20% most central Cu

